./.research/260720_compile-only-build-drivers.md:609:The driver identifier is versioned (`go-v1`), so any change to command arguments, environment, sandbox-relevant semantics, receipt interpretation, or output rules requires a new driver identifier or an explicitly versioned cache-key policy revision.
./.research/260720_compile-only-build-drivers.md:611:Retain the prior marker-embed case as a **negative migration/regression fixture**, not as a valid v1 command. It uses a root module, so the new `build_roots` rule rejects it before cache-key construction. The two raw snapshots share `go.mod` and this source and differ only in root `.csk-install.json`:
