./.task-board/EPIC-260720-21aq1i_declarative-compiled-builds/STORY-260720-3plyvy_curator-go-build-driver/TASK-260720-1zntv0_implement-go-v1-preflight-and-build/README.md:1:# Implement go-v1 preflight and artifact build
./.task-board/EPIC-260720-21aq1i_declarative-compiled-builds/STORY-260720-3plyvy_curator-go-build-driver/TASK-260720-1zntv0_implement-go-v1-preflight-and-build/README.md:4:Implement the source-aware go-v1 pipeline that validates the complete active package graph with one fixed go list command, builds with one fixed go build command, verifies the staged executable, and never transfers control to package code.
./.task-board/EPIC-260720-21aq1i_declarative-compiled-builds/STORY-260720-3plyvy_curator-go-build-driver/TASK-260720-1zntv0_implement-go-v1-preflight-and-build/README.md:7:Continue in internal/godriver using the trusted session and frozen build source. Set CWD to canonical source_dir and expose a build-tagged host-execution policy boundary. Present the validated snapshot and vendored module tree read-only; allow writes only below operation-private Go cache, temp, telemetry, and output roots; enforce the empty fixed environment and network/module/VCS denial on every platform; and apply supported host deadlines plus bounded output, artifact/disk, memory, and process controls without widening the executable graph. Parse the complete fixed go list stream; require one non-DepOnly main package and validate every standard input below fingerprinted GOROOT and every non-standard module, source, embed, and dependency input below build_root. Reject errors, incomplete packages, cgo and native fields, every SysoFiles entry, non-standard SFiles, and the exact ASCII //go:cgo_import_dynamic token in active non-standard GoFiles. Build only with the normative internal-link, no-libgcc argv into private staging. Verify one bounded regular output, apply manager permissions, hash it, and expose artifact metadata. Do not publish caches, write markers, or execute the artifact.
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-12iigs/TASK-260720-12iigs_results.md:5:Implemented strict build-receipt-v1 and install-marker-v2 schemas, shared build-source/target/toolchain/policy/input/artifact/build-record definitions, conditional build_source semantics, positive and negative generated cases, index entries, manifest hashes, and marker-v1 freeze tests. Receipt cases reject provenance booleans and physical cache, receipt, and lock paths. Marker v2 supports skill schemas 0 through 6 and generated cases cover empty and non-empty build metadata. Draft 2020-12 cannot express generic lexical ordering for arbitrary values or object keys; protocol prose remains normative for writer sorting, while generator tests assert sorted build_roots and emitted builds keys.
./.task-board/EPIC-260720-21aq1i_declarative-compiled-builds/STORY-260720-3plyvy_curator-go-build-driver/TASK-260720-1zntv0_implement-go-v1-preflight-and-build/progress.md:33:- [TASK-260720-1zntv0_go-v1-execution-boundary.puml](file://TASK-260720-1zntv0/TASK-260720-1zntv0_go-v1-execution-boundary.puml) — PlantUML source for the fixed process graph, readonly inputs, writable roots, denied surfaces, and host controls
./.task-board/EPIC-260720-21aq1i_declarative-compiled-builds/STORY-260720-3plyvy_curator-go-build-driver/TASK-260720-1zntv0_implement-go-v1-preflight-and-build/progress.md:34:- [TASK-260720-1zntv0_go-v1-execution-boundary.svg](file://TASK-260720-1zntv0/TASK-260720-1zntv0_go-v1-execution-boundary.svg) — Rendered go-v1 execution and isolation boundary
./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-3lo9jc/TASK-260720-3lo9jc_results.md:10:The schema index now provides a complete schema 6 declaration, canonical and legacy compatibility, exact receipt/marker/claim schemas and vectors, fixed go-v1 prerequisites, and the future-driver standardization process. The conformance contract now defines rc.4 manager evidence, fixture/vector execution, suite hash semantics, claim v1/v2 handling, and fail-closed behavior. The Curator CLI guide now covers install/upgrade builds, context exclusion, cache and marker currentness, compiler-free dry-run results, diagnostics, repair, GC, security limits, and the absence of package argv/hooks or generic build options without claiming an existing manager release ships schema 6.
./.task-board/EPIC-260720-21aq1i_declarative-compiled-builds/STORY-260720-35dck7_protocol-schema-v6/TASK-260720-1s1vr6_build-driver-conformance-vectors/README.md:1:# Generate go-v1 build-driver conformance vectors
./.task-board/EPIC-260720-21aq1i_declarative-compiled-builds/STORY-260720-35dck7_protocol-schema-v6/TASK-260720-1s1vr6_build-driver-conformance-vectors/README.md:10:Positive vectors cover schema 6 build_roots, mixed script and build commands, build-source exclusion while unrelated context remains visible, valid vendor-only main packages, all five direct Go argv forms, fixed environment, protected cache hit, compiler-free dry-run miss, and exact CCJ-1 build input, cache key, stored receipt, receipt hash, marker, artifact identity, curator-build-source-v1 bytes, and curator-go-toolchain-v1 bytes; build-source vectors exercise the domain prefix, unsigned UTF-8 ordering, uint64be framing, empty and binary files, root .csk-install.json, mode and timestamp non-inputs, invalid Unicode, duplicate paths, links and special files, mutation during use, and the legacy NUL-stream structural-collision regression; toolchain vectors exercise unsorted files, directories and internal links, LF and CRLF version normalization, mode and timestamp non-inputs, malformed version output, invalid Unicode, duplicate paths, escaping links, a selected executable outside GOROOT, and tree mutation; negative vectors cover schema 5, unknown driver and forbidden fields, missing unused overlapping or runtime-overlapping roots, root or escaped source, links and special files, nested module, non-main or multiple package, missing or inconsistent vendor data, workspace or toolchain switching, unsupported Go family, cgo and native inputs, syso, assembly includes, escaped embed inputs, go:cgo_import_dynamic, generators, PGO, poisoned environment and fake Go, telemetry failure, external-link or libgcc fallback, toolchain path and digest failures, cache key or target or receipt or artifact corruption, noncanonical receipt, concurrent publisher, forged self-consistent receipt outside protected state, and marker-embed build-source regression; cache-hit and dry-run context vectors run no source-aware Go commands; generation is deterministic, go test ./tools/generate-vectors passes, and existing script-fixture and registry expected hashes remain unchanged.
